hermes-jev-skills
-----------------
Copyright Steve Darlow.
Licensed under the MIT License.
https://github.com/kerpopule/hermes-jev-skills

hermes-jev-skills is NOT bundled here. It is the consumer this bridge is built
for, and `laya-for-agents setup-hermes` clones it from upstream on demand into
`vendor/hermes-jev-skills` (gitignored, so the copy always tracks upstream
rather than a stale vendored snapshot).

The tests in `tests/test_lfa_engine.py` named `JevValidatorTests` restate the
reply invariants that project's `jevkit/client.py` enforces on a decision
model's response, so a change here that would silently start failing on the
client is caught locally. They are an independent restatement of a documented
interface, not copied code.


TypeSafe Jev
------------
Jev is a product of TypeSafe AI.
https://docs.typesafe.ai

The `/v1/systemone` wire protocol implemented here is TypeSafe's. This project
implements the protocol, not the model, and is not affiliated with, endorsed by
or sponsored by TypeSafe AI. Laya implements the same protocol for its own
weights, and this fork serves Laya's.
